{"id":"resp_86115e945dac0463","created_at":1795618540,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_88f2e6e486cb3830","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes that enforce the requirement: internal structures within ice strengthened hull areas must have a corrosion abrasion addition ts = 1.0 mm. The ontology provides properties: internalStructure, internalIceStrengthenedStructure, hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure, internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition (object property linking internalIceStrengthenedStructure to QuantityValue). Also corrosionAbrasionAddition property (maybe generic). The requirement applies to Polar Class ships; we have property polarClassRequirementsApplicable (boolean) on ship, and polarClass (object property linking ship to polarClassValue). But unclear target.\n\nAdmission says focus_set owner_class is ship. So SHACL target should be ship instances. But need to enforce that for each ship where polarClassRequirementsApplicable true (or polarClass is any PC?), the internal structures in ice strengthened hull areas have corrosion abrasion addition of at least 1.0 mm.\n\nWe have no data instances but need shape definitions. Use sh:targetClass https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship.\n\nConstraint: for each ship, if polarClassRequirementsApplicable true (or we could check polarClass property existence?), then we need to traverse hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure to internalIceStrengthenedStructure, then internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition to a QuantityValue node which must have numericValue = 1.0 and unit = mm.\n\nUse sh:property with sh:path to a nested path? SHACL allows sh:property with sh:path (can be a sequence via sh:alternativePath, but just we can use blank node with sh:qualifiedValueShape? Simpler: use sh:property with sh:path [sh:inversePath?]. Maybe easier: use sh:property with sh:path (hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure / internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition / qudt:numericValue) using sh:property path of sh:property also can be a sequence via sh:or?\n\nStandard SHACL uses sh:path can be an RDF list via sh:inversePath and sh:zeroOrMorePath etc (SPARQL property paths). Actually SHACL core supports sh:path as an RDF list syntax representing arbitrary property paths? I think SHACL 1.0 allows sh:path to be a property or an rdf:list of properties meaning sequence (? subject ?p1 ?mid . ?mid ?p2 ?value). So we can define.\n\nThus shape:\n\n_:corrosionAdditionShape a sh:NodeShape;\n  sh:targetClass nltl:ship;\n  sh:property [\n    sh:path ( nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition qudt:numericValue );\n    sh:equals 1.0? Use sh:hasValue with literal? Or sh:equals? There's sh:hasValue constraint for a specific value. Use sh:hasValue 1.0 typed decimal. But need unit as well. So we need qualified value shape: sh:property with sh:path (nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition) and then sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNode? Then we need nested shape for QuantityValue: with sh:property numericValue=1.0 and unit=mm.\n\nSimplify: Use sh:property for path to internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition and then sh:node shape referencing another shape.\n\nDefine shape for QuantityValue: nltl:QuantityValueShape with targetClass qudt:QuantityValue maybe not needed.\n\nQuantityValue shape:\n\n _:qShape a sh:NodeShape;\n   sh:property [\n     sh:path qudt:numericValue;\n     sh:datatype xsd:decimal;\n     sh:minInclusive 1.0;\n     sh:maxInclusive 1.0;\n   ];\n   sh:property [\n     sh:path qudt:unit;\n     sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM>;\n   ].\n\nNow main ship shape includes conditional activation: only if polarization applicable. Use sh:if? There's sh:targetNode/property? Not directly. Use sh:rule? But SHACL does not have conditional. Use sh:property with sh:or? Could define two shapes: one for ships with polarClassRequirementsApplicable true (sh:property with sh:path polarClassRequirementsApplicable and sh:hasValue true) and then combine via sh:node? Alternatively use sh:targetSubjectsOf for polarClassRequirementsApplicable? Actually could target based on that property: sh:targetSubjectsOf nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable and then apply constraints. That would only target ships that have that property. However the property may be true literal. Could also require value true using sh:nodeKind? No.\n\nBetter: create a shape that targets ships (sh:targetClass) and includes a sh:property that only applies when polarClassRequirementsApplicable true: use sh:qualifiedValueShape with sh:qualifiedMinCount 1 maybe. Not straightforward. Simpler: we can assert that any ship must have internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition 1.0 mm, regardless of polar class. That might be over-constraining but spec not ask to enforce applicability condition? Requirement says Polar Class ships are to have. Could enforce only for ships where polarClassRequirementsApplicable true, but we may note ambiguity.\n\nWe must \"Record material ambiguity instead of guessing.\" Since applicability conditional not fully defined (no explicit activation condition captured), we should note ambiguity. Perhaps create SHACL shape with rdfs:comment indicating ambiguous applicability.\n\nThus produce shape with targetClass ship, property path as described, and comment. No attempt to condition.\n\nAlso include shape for internalIceStrengthenedStructure maybe.\n\nImplement using prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, nltl, qudt.\n\nNow produce final Turtle with shapes.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_865b727ec14e6feb","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape: QuantityValue – represents the corrosion/abrasion addition\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:QuantityValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    rdfs:comment \"QuantityValue node that must encode the corrosion/abrasion addition as exactly 1.0 mm per I2‑11.3. Units and datatype are fixed by the locked representation context.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:maxInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Numeric value must be exactly 1.0 (decimal), per the source requirement.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:MilliM ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Unit must be the canonical QUDT millimetre unit.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape: Ship – applies the corrosion/abrasion addition requirement\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ShipCorrosionAbrasionAdditionShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    rdfs:comment \"\"\"\n    This shape encodes the requirement from I2‑11.3:\n    “Polar Class ships are to have a minimum corrosion/abrasion addition of ts = 1.0 mm applied to all internal structures within the ice‑strengthened hull areas…”.\n    \n    The applicability to Polar‑Class ships is recorded in the source but the exact activation condition\n    (e.g., presence/true value of nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable) is ambiguous in the supplied data.\n    Consequently, this shape validates the numeric/units constraints for every ship instance; callers may\n    apply additional filtering based on their own eligibility assertions.\n    \"\"\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        # Path: ship → internalIceStrengthenedStructure → corrosion addition quantity value\n        sh:path ( nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition ) ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Each internal ice‑strengthened structure linked from a ship must have an associated corrosion/abrasion addition matching the QuantityValueShape.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape: InternalIceStrengthenedStructure – optional sanity check\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:InternalIceStrengthenedStructureShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:internalIceStrengthenedStructure ;\n    rdfs:comment \"Internal ice‑strengthened structures should be linked from a ship via nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure. No further constraints are required beyond the QuantityValueShape enforced on the ship.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition ;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;\n        rdfs:comment \"The corrosion abrasion addition property must point to a QuantityValue (validated by the QuantityValueShape).\" ;\n    ] .\n\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":24208,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":23600,"input_tokens_per_turn":[24208],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":2011,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1194,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[2011],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":26219},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}